<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Made of twigs</i> or <i>osiers</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calathisci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					64, 320</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to virga, II. C.) <i>Striped</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sagula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 660</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					4, 155</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tigris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 344</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Herc. Oet. 146</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgato corpore tigris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					5, 148</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nurus,</span>”
				<i>in striped garments</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 159</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
